# Inspection notes: Data_deposition_RNAseq_Paroxetine_2017.xlsx

## Sheets
- Mapping_statistics: 91 rows x 22 cols (header row0 + 90 samples)
- NormCount: 25406 rows x 188 cols (25402 genes)

## Mapping_statistics (authoritative metadata = cols 0-10)
Index, Sample ID, total read, NH:i:1(mapped), HI:I:0(unmapped), mapping rate,
Response, Tissue, Code, DESeq(count filename), Index_DESeq(1-90)
Cols 11-21 = duplicated/artifact columns (repeat NH/HI/mapping/total, CSV fragments,
"Over represented sequences (fastqc)", extra Sample ID, extra mapping rate).
90 samples = 3 Tissue x 3 Response x 10 reps
  Tissue: baseline_blood, dentate_gyrus, final_blood
  Response: Control, good_responder, bad_responder

## NormCount layout
Row1 block labels: baseline blood@col2, dentate gyrus@col32, final blood@col62,
  Max@92-94, Median@95-97, DESeq Comparison1-9@98.., Comparison1-9@179-187
Row4 headers: Index(0), GeneID(1), 90 sample CPM cols (2-91, 30/tissue),
  Max(92-94), Median(95-97), 9 DESeq blocks(98-178), 9 summary DEG(179-187)
Each DESeq block (9 cols): baseMean, baseMeanA, baseMeanB, foldChange,
  log2FoldChange, pval, padj, DEG, DEG.  (2nd DEG col == Comparison1-9 summary col)
Sample cols = normalized counts (CPM-like floats). GeneID unique (25402).
DESeq numeric cols contain 'NA','=-Inf','=Inf' specials.
DEG markers: 'U' up, 'D' down, '-' not.

## KEY: file ALREADY contains DE results (log2FC,pval,padj,baseMean,DEG) for 9 comparisons.
Raw counts NOT in file (only CPM + DESeq summaries) -> cannot re-run DESeq2 from raw.

## 9 comparisons grouping (by tissue-divergence: NA/Inf count, frac|log2FC|>1)
Comp1-3: dentate-involved (NA~4600, frac|lfc|>1~0.125)
Comp4-6: blood-vs-blood (NA~3370 lowest, frac|lfc|>1~0.08) -> ~ Final vs Baseline
Comp7-9: dentate-involved (NA~5140 highest, frac|lfc|>1~0.127)
Mapping the 2 dentate pairs (DG vs Baseline / DG vs Final) NOT fully resolvable.

